n/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+3)}\\,x(-3) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7(t+3)} & (t+3){e}^{7(t+3)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7(t+3)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,(-2t-6){e}^{7(t+3)}\\, \\\\ \\,-2{e}^{7(t+3)}\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a22e898-470d-5e85-9a6c-1224cd8777f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a22e898-470d-5e85-9a6c-1224cd8777f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309570} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b0e62b0-582b-5d3a-9477-33f4077f2b98" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f8550c3-f522-5258-8e0b-73324de5b1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f8550c3-f522-5258-8e0b-73324de5b1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310036} :answer-field/id #uuid "e95a834d-03cb-586d-9850-7d2b0447898e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7870a76-0c90-529a-9ddb-a95d0acab0af" :question/math-academy-id "q-335437" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-8x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-1) \\\\ y(-1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+1)}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1))\\, \\\\ \\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05145451-fcbb-5f80-80f4-d64ca99158d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308785} {:answer/i